ribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\pm 2x"] ["math" "y=\\pm 4x"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{1}{2}x"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{1}{4}x"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{1}{8}x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "fca551999182ae333663420d91dc543dd930ece33ac0822929585890a6c50f30"} {"question" "q-10431" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\pm \\frac{1}{2}x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "fca551999182ae333663420d91dc543dd930ece33ac0822929585890a6c50f30"} {"question" "q-316963" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The asymptotes of the hyperbola $\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{100}=1$ are$\\,\\,y=\\pm $\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "fca551999182ae333663420d91dc543dd930ece33ac0822929585890a6c50f30"} {"question" "q-316963" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\na=\\sqrt{4}=2,\\,b=\\sqrt{100}=10.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\frac{2}{10}x \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{1}{5}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "fca551999182ae333663420d91dc543dd930ece33ac0822929585890a6c50f30"} {"question" "q-316963" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "60aeffb4230af503f600c2fcc10b85051688f94a5758300b6b5620fe9231f141"} {"question" "q-316963" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "fca551999182ae333663420d91dc543dd930ece33ac0822929585890a6c50f30"} {"question" "q-316963" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{5}x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "fca551999182ae333663420d91dc543dd930ece33ac0822929585890a6c50f30"} {"question" "q-316965" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The asymptotes of the hyperbola $\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{36}=1$ are$\\,\\,y=\\pm $\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "fca551999182ae333663420d91dc543dd930ece33ac0822929585890a6c50f30"} {"question" "q-316965" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\na=\\sqrt{16}=4,\\,b=\\sqrt{36}=6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\frac{4}{6}x \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{2}{3}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "fca551999182ae333663420d91dc543dd930ece33ac0822929585890a6c50f30"} {"question" "q-316965" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "60aeffb4230af503f600c2fcc10b85051688f94a5758300b6b5620fe9231f141"} {"question" "q-316965" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "fca551999182ae333663420d91dc543dd930ece33ac0822929585890a6c50f30"} {"question" "q-316965" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{3}x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "fca551999182ae333663420d91dc543dd930ece33ac0822929585890a6c50f30"} {"question" "q-316942" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The asymptotes of the hyperbola ${x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}=8$ are$\\,\\,y=\\pm $\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "fca551999182ae333663420d91dc543dd930ece33ac0822929585890a6c50f30"} {"question" "q-316942" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}x.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the given equation in standard form, we divide both sides of the equation by $8$ and then simplify, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2} & =8 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{2{y}^{2}}{8} & =\\frac{8}{8} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have $a=\\sqrt{8}$ and $b=\\sqrt{4}=2.$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{8}}x \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{2}{2\\sqrt{2}}x \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}x \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "fca551999182ae333663420d91dc543dd930ece33ac0822929585890a6c50f30"} {"question" "q-316942" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "60aeffb4230af503f600c2fcc10b85051688f94a5758300b6b5620fe9231f141"} {"question" "q-316942" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "fca551999182ae333663420d91dc543dd930ece33ac0822929585890a6c50f30"} {"question" "q-316942" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "fca551999182ae333663420d91dc543dd930ece33ac0822929585890a6c50f30"} {"question" "q-7973" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the asymptotes of the hyperbola $25{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}=100.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "fca551999182ae333663420d91dc543dd930ece33ac0822929585890a6c50f30"} {"question" "q-7973" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}x.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the given equation in standard form, we divide both sides of the equation by $100$ and then simplify, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2} & =100 \\\\ \\frac{25{x}^{2}}{100}-\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{100} & =\\frac{100}{100} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have $a=\\sqrt{4}=2,$ and $b=\\sqrt{25}=5.$ \n\nTherefore, the asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\frac{5}{2}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "fca551999182ae333663420d91dc543dd930ece33ac0822929585890a6c50f30"} {"question" "q-7973" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "60aeffb4230af503f600c2fcc10b85051688f94a5758300b6b5620fe9231f141"} {"question" "q-7973" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "fca551999182ae333663420d91dc543dd930ece33ac0822929585890a6c50f30"} {"question" "q-7973" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{2}{5}x"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{3}{2}x"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{3}{4}x"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{5}{2}x"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{5}{4}x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "fca551999182ae333663420d91dc543dd930ece33ac0822929585890a6c50f30"} {"question" "q-7973" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\pm \\frac{5}{2}x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "fca551999182ae333663420d91dc543dd930ece33ac0822929585890a6c50f30"} {"question" "q-10438" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the asymptotes of the hyperbola $25{y}^{2}-4{x}^{2}=100.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "fca551999182ae333663420d91dc543dd930ece33ac0822929585890a6c50f30"} {"question" "q-10438" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{a}{b}x.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the given equation in standard form, we divide both sides of the equation by $100$ and then simplify, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25{y}^{2}-4{x}^{2} & =100 \\\\ \\frac{25{y}^{2}}{100}-\\frac{4{x}^{2}}{100} & =\\frac{100}{100} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have $a=\\sqrt{4}=2$ and $b=\\sqrt{25}=5.$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are $y=\\pm \\frac{2}{5}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "fca551999182ae333663420d91dc543dd930ece33ac0822929585890a6c50f30"} {"question" "q-10438" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "60aeffb4230af503f600c2fcc10b85051688f94a5758300b6b5620fe9231f141"} {"question" "q-10438" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "fca551999182ae333663420d91dc543dd930ece33ac0822929585890a6c50f30"} {"question" "q-10438" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{2}{5}x"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{3}{5}x"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{4}{5}x"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{5}{2}x"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{5}{4}x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "fca551999182ae333663420d91dc543dd930ece33ac0822929585890a6c50f30"} {"question" "q-10438" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\pm \\frac{2}{5}x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "fca551999182ae333663420d91dc543dd930ece33ac0822929585890a6c50f30"} {"question" "q-7975" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the asymptotes of the hyperbola $25{x}^{2}-16{y}^{2}=400.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "fca551999182ae333663420d91dc543dd930ece33ac0822929585890a6c50f30"} {"question" "q-7975" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}x.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the given equation in standard form, we divide both sides of the equation by $400$ and then simplify, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25{x}^{2}-16{y}^{2} & =400 \\\\ \\frac{25{x}^{2}}{400}-\\frac{16{y}^{2}}{400} & =\\frac{400}{400} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have $a=\\sqrt{16}=4,$ and $b=\\sqrt{25}=5.$ \n\nTherefore, the asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\frac{5}{4}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "fca551999182ae333663420d91dc543dd930ece33ac0822929585890a6c50f30"} {"question" "q-7975" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "60aeffb4230af503f600c2fcc10b85051688f94a5758300b6b5620fe9231f141"} {"question" "q-7975" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "fca551999182ae333663420d91dc543dd930ece33ac0822929585890a6c50f30"} {"question" "q-7975" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{2}{5}x"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{4}{5}x"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{5}{2}x"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{5}{4}x"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\frac{5}{8}x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "fca551999182ae333663420d91dc543dd930ece33ac0822929585890a6c50f30"} {"question" "q-7975" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\pm \\frac{5}{4}x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "fca551999182ae333663420d91dc543dd930ece33ac0822929585890a6c50f30"} {"question" "q-316934" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The asymptotes of the hyperbola $8{x}^{2}-50{y}^{2}=400$ are$\\,\\,y=\\pm $\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "fca551999182ae333663420d91dc543dd930ece33ac0822929585890a6c50f30"} {"question" "q-316934" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}x.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the given equation in standard form, we divide both sides of the equation by $400$ and then simplify, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{x}^{2}-50{y}^{2} & =400 \\\\ \\frac{8{x}^{2}}{400}-\\frac{50{y}^{2}}{400} & =\\frac{400}{400} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{50}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have $a=\\sqrt{50}$ and $b=\\sqrt{8}.$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{8}}{\\sqrt{50}}x \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{5\\sqrt{2}}x \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{2}{5}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "fca551999182ae333663420d91dc543dd930ece33ac0822929585890a6c50f30"} {"question" "q-316934" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "60aeffb4230af503f600c2fcc10b85051688f94a5758300b6b5620fe9231f141"} {"question" "q-316934" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "fca551999182ae333663420d91dc543dd930ece33ac0822929585890a6c50f30"} {"question" "q-316934" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{5}x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/state.json" "file_sha256" "fca551999182ae333663420d91dc543dd930ece33ac0822929585890a6c50f30"} {"question" "e-7426" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the asymptotes of the hyperbola $\\dfrac{x^2}{36} - \\dfrac{y^2}{9} = 1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/example-7426.json" "file_sha256" "5d71748f6b1f177ed65bf13153afef1c044de51fb98d0ad1b8050ef1b9a87631"} {"question" "e-7426" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{x^2}{a^2} - \\frac{y^2}{b^2}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\dfrac{b}{a}x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\na=\\sqrt{36} = 6, \\qquad b=\\sqrt9 =3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm \\frac{3}{6}x \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{1}{2}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/example-7426.json" "file_sha256" "5d71748f6b1f177ed65bf13153afef1c044de51fb98d0ad1b8050ef1b9a87631"} {"question" "e-5356" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the asymptotes of the hyperbola $\\dfrac{y^2}{9} - \\dfrac{x^2}{16} = 1$." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/example-5356.json" "file_sha256" "25b040ee46832290d03bb484b7bfd4d047c941cb3face9310434bdb6c6f3c527"} {"question" "e-5356" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{y^2}{a^2} - \\dfrac{x^2}{b^2} = 1.\n$$\n\nFor a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\dfrac{a}{b} x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\na=\\sqrt{9} = 3, \\qquad b=\\sqrt{16} = 4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are $y = \\pm \\dfrac{3}{4}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/example-5356.json" "file_sha256" "25b040ee46832290d03bb484b7bfd4d047c941cb3face9310434bdb6c6f3c527"} {"question" "e-5357" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the asymptotes of the hyperbola $25 x ^ 2 - 9 y ^ 2 = 225$." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/example-5357.json" "file_sha256" "ad7390d334eda1212106cbed5c0e778997bd5b7318b551c86d65463d0a921b12"} {"question" "e-5357" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The standard equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{x^2}{a^2} - \\frac{y^2}{b^2}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\dfrac{b}{a}x.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the given equation in standard form, we divide both sides of the equation by $225$ and then simplify, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}25{x}^{2}-9{y}^{2} & =225 \\\\ \\frac{25{x}^{2}}{225}-\\frac{9{y}^{2}}{225} & =\\frac{225}{225} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have $a=\\sqrt 9 = 3,$ and $b=\\sqrt{25} = 5.$ \n\nTherefore, the asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\dfrac{5}{3}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14053302/example-5357.json" "file_sha256" "ad7390d334eda1212106cbed5c0e778997bd5b7318b551c86d65463d0a921b12"}] "usage" {"e-5357" [] "e-7426" [] "e-5356" []} "basis" 1776 "retractions" [[17592186087566 :question/problem "Find the asymptotes of the hyperbola $\\dfrac{x^2}{36} - \\dfrac{y^2}{9} = 1$."] [17592186087566 :question/worked-solution "The standard equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{x^2}{a^2} - \\frac{y^2}{b^2}=1\n$$\n\nFor a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\dfrac{b}{a}x\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\na=\\sqrt{36} = 6, \\qquad b=\\sqrt9 =3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &= ± \\frac{3}{6}x \\\\\n&= ± \\frac{1}{2}x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186087485 :question/worked-solution "The standard equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{y^2}{a^2} - \\dfrac{x^2}{b^2} = 1\n$$\n\nFor a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\dfrac{a}{b} x\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\na=\\sqrt{9} = 3, \\qquad b=\\sqrt{16} = 4\n$$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes of the hyperbola are\n\n$$\ny = \\pm \\dfrac{3}{4}x\n$$"] [17592186087486 :question/worked-solution "The standard equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{x^2}{a^2} - \\frac{y^2}{b^2}=1\n$$\n\nFor a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\dfrac{b}{a}x\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the given equation in standard form, we divide both sides of the equation by $225$ and then simplify, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n25x^{2} - 9y^{2} &= 225 \\\\\n\\frac{25x^{2}}{225} - \\frac{9y^{2}}{225} &= \\frac{225}{225} \\\\\n\\frac{x^{2}}{9} - \\frac{y^{2}}{25} &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\na=\\sqrt 9 = 3\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nb=\\sqrt{25} = 5\n$$\n\nTherefore, the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\dfrac{5}{3}x\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
